.TH TRUE 1 "September 19, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
true \- provide a successful truth value
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B true
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I True
does nothing, successfully.
It is typically used in input to
.IR sh (1),
such as:
.PP
.B while true; do echo tick; sleep 1; done
.SH FILES
/usr/man/TRUE  this page
.SH "SEE ALSO"
false(1), sh(1), licenses(1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Exit status is 0.
